decision: changes-requested

Three medium-severity blockers remain:

- **R2-F6:** HEAD-resolution failures still silently suppress the check.
- **R2-F7:** The probe interprets filenames as Git pathspecs, producing false recommendations.
- **R2-F8:** The remediation cannot satisfy the check when Git configuration disables filter reads.

R1-F2, R1-F3 and R1-F4 are fixed. R1-F5 is partially fixed.

Applied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed the sealed scope, implementation, tests, CI and validation registration. Read-only Git probes confirmed the configuration and pathspec behavior; [Git’s implementation](https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.56.0/revision.c) and [configuration documentation](https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.56.0/Documentation/config/commitgraph.adoc) support those conclusions. Package tests and validation use the supplied sealed evidence. Artifact and surface checks returned successfully. The repository remains unchanged.

